As consciousness slowly returns, the protagonist staggers to his feet, brushing away layers of golden sand. The devastated landscape stretches endlessly before him—towering dunes that seem to touch the sky, their surfaces carved by winds that howl with an otherworldly fury. In the distance, through the haze of a sandstorm, a silhouette emerges.

A figure approaches, moving with deliberate purpose through the wasteland. This is Kael, a legendary hero whispered about in ancient texts—one of the few who learned to master the elements before the great cataclysm. His weathered face tells stories of countless battles, and his eyes glow faintly with the power of controlled fire, a stark contrast to the oppressive sand all around.

"You've finally awakened," Kael's voice cuts through the wind like a blade. He extends his hand, a warm aura of flames dancing around his palm. "The world was not always like this. Once, we had balance—humans who could bend earth, water, wind, and fire in harmony. But greed corrupted that gift. The element wars consumed everything."

The protagonist realizes he has no memory of who he is or how he came to be buried in this sand. Kael's expression softens with recognition, as if he knows something vital about this stranger. "Come. There are others like us—element wielders who refuse to accept this end. We gather in the last sanctuary, hidden beneath the sands. If you're willing to fight, to learn, and to reclaim what was lost, then your awakening may be the sign we've been waiting for."

With that, Kael extends his hand once more, waiting for the protagonist to choose his destiny.
